      '**Beta-adrenergic blockers** (names ending in **-olol**) block β receptors. They slow the heart and lower blood pressure, and treat hypertension, angina, heart failure (specific drugs), arrhythmias, migraine prevention and performance anxiety. **Cardioselective** blockers (metoprolol, atenolol; remember “A through M”) mainly block β1. **Nonselective** blockers (propranolol, nadolol) also block β2, which can trigger **bronchospasm** in people with asthma or COPD.',
